<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Victual Brothers</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1392">1392</a>–<a href="/years/1401">1401</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Vitalienbrüder, Likedeelers</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Victual Brothers were privateers, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a>, who first appeared in 1392 supplying besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stockholm">Stockholm</a> for Albert of Mecklenburg against Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margaret-i-of-denmark">Margaret I</a>. They then preyed on Hanseatic shipping in the Baltic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a>, occupying Gotland until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> expelled them in 1398. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a> fleets defeated them in 1400–1401 and executed their leaders, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klaus-stortebeker">Klaus Störtebeker</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/victual-brothers.jpg" alt="Victual Brothers" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vitalienbrueder,_Wandmalerei_in_d,_Kirche_zu_Bunge_auf_Gotland,_gemalt_ca._1405.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
